``` LF-07 | Heavy Forwarder Backpressure: Output Blocked to Indexers
    Splunk Administrator Field Manual - Gaurav Malik

    Use case: A heavy forwarder or intermediate forwarder is falling behind;
    confirm whether its output to the indexers is blocked, to which
    destinations, and for how long.
    Run on: SH, with the forwarder's _internal forwarded. A fully blocked
    forwarder may not be able to send its own logs; if nothing shows up, check
    splunkd.log on the box.
    Query: Output queue fill on the forwarder (SH)
    If this returns nothing, run probes/LF-07-probe.spl to confirm the data it
    reads exists here.
```
index=_internal source=*metrics.log group=queue earliest=-4h
    (name=tcpout_* OR name=parsingqueue OR name=indexqueue)
| eval fill_pct=round(100 * current_size_kb / max_size_kb, 1)
| timechart span=5m max(fill_pct) by name
